sargo SDHCI: multi-block reads, 8-bit bus and 52 MHz, each verified

Reads were one 512-byte CMD17 per command on a 1-bit bus at 25 MHz, with
a DAT reset each time; the first boot needed ~30 min to reach the Apple
logo. After the partition lookup, sargo_speed_up() takes a reference copy
of LBA 0..63 the old way, then enables CMD18 + Auto CMD12 reads of up to
128 KiB through a page-wise ADMA2 table, an 8-bit (else 4-bit) bus and
52 MHz high-speed timing. Each step re-reads LBA 0..63 and is undone if
the data differs. A read error later drops back to 1-bit 25 MHz, and
three more to single-block reads. RAM-overlay sectors (0086) still win
over eMMC data. Boot-args: sargo_mb=0, sargo_bus=1|4|8, sargo_hs=0.

--- a/bsd/dev/sargo_sdhci.c
